      en: "Przemyśl (German: Premissel) is a city in the Subcarpathian Voivodeship, near the Ukrainian border. Founded in the 10th century, it was a major trading center on the east-west route. The Old Town is dominated by the Cathedral of the Assumption of the Virgin Mary and the Castle of the Przemyśl dukes. The city has a turbulent history between Poland, Austria-Hungary, and Ukraine. The Przemyśl Fortress was one of the largest fortresses in Europe during World War I. Today, the city has about 62,000 inhabitants on an area of 44 km². The economy is based on services and tourism. The multilingual population shapes the cultural life.",
